    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country E.164 national-number length validation in the owner-creation path.\n\n**The problem.** The `POST /api/owners` handler normalizes telephones to E.164 via `toE164(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. The old logic assumed `+61` for *every* bare number and only enforced a loose 8\u201315 total-digit bound \u2014 so it had no notion of national-number length per country code.\n\n**The change** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- `toE164` now detects the country code: a leading `+` is kept as-is; a bare number in national trunk form (leading `0`) is treated as Australian (`+61`, dropping the `0`); any other bare number is treated as NANP (`+1`). This reclassification was necessary because the existing suite creates owners with bare 10-digit NANP numbers like `6085550000` \u2014 under the old blanket `+61` assumption those become 10 national digits, which the new `+61`-requires-9 rule would wrongly reject.\n- A new `hasValidNationalLength` helper enforces the rule: `+61` requires exactly **9** national digits, `+1` requires exactly **10**; other country codes keep only the general 8\u201315 bound. A wrong length returns `null`, which the handler already maps to **400 Bad Request**.\n\n**Docs.** Updated the `telephone` field description in `openapi.yml` to describe the refined normalization and the per-country length rule.\n\n**Verification.** The new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`+61 123` \u2192 3 national digits \u2192 400) passes, all 29 existing owner controller tests (bare NANP numbers \u2192 `+1`, still 201) pass, and the entire 262-test suite is green.",
